  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37130526",
      "title": "Understanding Classes",
      "lectureOrder": 35,
      "videoOrder": 32,
      "sourceHash": "439f58a9f2215fc15f4eaf44172a7ac1173ec49cf6822850d81daf510b116645",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 5.19,
          "en": "As you learned, widgets are objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.19,
          "end": 8.64,
          "en": "And objects are simply these data structures in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.64,
          "end": 11.01,
          "en": "And of course, not just widgets are objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.01,
          "end": 12.15,
          "en": "As you learned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.15,
          "end": 16.41,
          "en": "all value types in the end are also objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.41,
          "end": 20.13,
          "en": "So all value types are such data structures in memory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.13,
          "end": 22.89,
          "en": "and that's why these objects concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.89,
          "end": 25.56,
          "en": "is a key concept in Dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.56,
          "end": 30.393,
          "en": "Now, classes are closely related to this objects concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.26,
          "end": 32.94,
          "en": "For that, it's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.94,
          "end": 36.24,
          "en": "that Dart is in the end, an object-oriented language,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.24,
          "end": 39.51,
          "en": "because as mentioned, every value is an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.51,
          "end": 42.09,
          "en": "And of course you have such primitive values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.09,
          "end": 46.44,
          "en": "like text or numbers, which are created by, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.44,
          "end": 49.17,
          "en": "wrapping text with single or double codes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.17,
          "end": 52.35,
          "en": "or simply writing down a number in your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.35,
          "end": 55.47,
          "en": "But you also have more complex values in your code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.47,
          "end": 57.36,
          "en": "like for example, these widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.36,
          "end": 60.3,
          "en": "but also these configuration objects, which you saw.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.3,
          "end": 62.4,
          "en": "For example, the object that allowed us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.4,
          "end": 67.05,
          "en": "to configure our gradient or the individual color objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.05,
          "end": 70.32,
          "en": "And those more complex values are created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.32,
          "end": 73.74,
          "en": "with help of classes, because classes in Dart,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.74,
          "end": 76.8,
          "en": "and in many other programming languages as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.8,
          "end": 80.01,
          "en": "are simply the blueprints for objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.01,
          "end": 83.34,
          "en": "Now, why do we need such blueprints though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.34,
          "end": 84.173,
          "en": "Well, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.173,
          "end": 87.45,
          "en": "objects are these data structures in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.45,
          "end": 89.458,
          "en": "And here a good question would be,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.458,
          "end": 92.61,
          "en": "what's inside these data structures?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.61,
          "end": 97.47,
          "en": "And the answer is data, so-called variables or properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.47,
          "end": 101.28,
          "en": "For example, the username of a logged in user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.28,
          "end": 104.46000000000001,
          "en": "or the color you chose for a gradient,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.46000000000001,
          "end": 107.72999999999999,
          "en": "but also logic functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.72999999999999,
          "end": 110.64,
          "en": "Or as it's typically called in the context of objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.64,
          "end": 112.41,
          "en": "so-called methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.41,
          "end": 117.038,
          "en": "So objects in the end are really all about organizing data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.038,
          "end": 118.77000000000001,
          "en": "and separating logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.77000000000001,
          "end": 121.53,
          "en": "so that logic that works with certain data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.53,
          "end": 124.74,
          "en": "is typically in the same object as that data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.74,
          "end": 126.45,
          "en": "and not in some other object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.45,
          "end": 128.76,
          "en": "or some other place in your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.76,
          "end": 131.91,
          "en": "For example, this color object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.91,
          "end": 134.79,
          "en": "will contain the different color values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.79,
          "end": 137.88,
          "en": "for its red, green, and blue colors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.88,
          "end": 140.01,
          "en": "And if you add a dot thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.01,
          "end": 144.15,
          "en": "which is the Dart syntax for accessing data or functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.15,
          "end": 148.5,
          "en": "that are grouped into an object, if you type such a dot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.5,
          "end": 151.71,
          "en": "you get a list of different variables, properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.71,
          "end": 152.7,
          "en": "that you can access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.7,
          "end": 154.47,
          "en": "So the data I just mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.47,
          "end": 156.18,
          "en": "that would be stored in the object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.18,
          "end": 158.94,
          "en": "the red, green and blue color values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.94,
          "end": 161.49,
          "en": "and some other pieces of data as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.49,
          "end": 165.12,
          "en": "But you for example, also get some functions down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.12,
          "end": 167.7,
          "en": "with blue, with green that, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.7,
          "end": 172.44,
          "en": "would allow you to create another color based on this color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.44,
          "end": 175.77,
          "en": "And which functions are provided by which object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.77,
          "end": 178.77,
          "en": "simply depends on the definition of this object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.77,
          "end": 181.71,
          "en": "And that's now where these classes become important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.71,
          "end": 185.94,
          "en": "because with those classes, you define exactly that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.94,
          "end": 189.66,
          "en": "You define which kind of data will be stored in an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.66,
          "end": 192.24,
          "en": "when it is then created at runtime,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.24,
          "end": 196.02,
          "en": "and you define which extra functions, so-called methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.02,
          "end": 198.48,
          "en": "might be stored in such a object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.48,
          "end": 201.81,
          "en": "So color here, like container and scaffold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.81,
          "end": 205.05,
          "en": "and box decoration, all these things are in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.05,
          "end": 208.82999999999998,
          "en": "classes, or when executed like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 208.82999999999998,
          "end": 212.73,
          "en": "or when using this from ARGB function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 212.73,
          "end": 214.29,
          "en": "you are in the end using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 214.29,
          "end": 217.38,
          "en": "so-called class constructor functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 217.38,
          "end": 219.63,
          "en": "which simply are functions that are used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.63,
          "end": 222.87,
          "en": "to create objects based on those classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 222.87,
          "end": 226.26,
          "en": "But all these things have classes as blueprints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 226.26,
          "end": 228.66,
          "en": "as you can also see in the official documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 228.66,
          "end": 231.81,
          "en": "This is the linear gradient class after all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 231.81,
          "end": 233.264,
          "en": "as you can see here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 233.264,
          "end": 237.99,
          "en": "And you see more classes that are related on the left.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 237.99,
          "end": 241.2,
          "en": "So these are all the blueprints that are built into Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 241.2,
          "end": 244.05,
          "en": "that you can use in your code to create objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 244.05,
          "end": 246.06,
          "en": "based on those blueprints.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 246.06,
          "end": 249.06,
          "en": "So in your code, you in the end work with the classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.06,
          "end": 251.25,
          "en": "and their constructor functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 251.25,
          "end": 254.34,
          "en": "and when your application then runs on a device,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 254.34,
          "end": 257.25,
          "en": "and your code executes from top to bottom,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 257.25,
          "end": 261.99,
          "en": "then the actual objects are created and stored in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 261.99,
          "end": 264.45,
          "en": "That's how you can think about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 264.45,
          "end": 266.7,
          "en": "So all these built-in widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 266.7,
          "end": 269.94,
          "en": "like these configuration objects here, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 269.94,
          "end": 273,
          "en": "are classes which you then turn into objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 273,
          "end": 275.19,
          "en": "by executing them like functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 275.19,
          "end": 278.73,
          "en": "So by calling their constructor functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 278.73,
          "end": 282.36,
          "en": "This process is also called class instantiation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 282.36,
          "end": 284.31,
          "en": "or object instantiation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 284.31,
          "end": 286.59000000000003,
          "en": "You are instantiating a class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 286.59000000000003,
          "end": 289.68,
          "en": "You are creating an object based on a class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 289.68,
          "end": 293.19,
          "en": "And that's why your custom widgets are also classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 293.19,
          "end": 295.98,
          "en": "The built-in widgets are defined as classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 295.98,
          "end": 299.313,
          "en": "You define your custom widgets also as classes.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
